WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.074
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.074 --> 00:00:03.412
It's Evan, my one word is believe

00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:05.427
and I believe in people
more than they believe

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:07.415
in themselves and my sincere hope is

00:00:07.415 --> 00:00:10.250
that if you see in
yourself, what I see in you,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.078
you'll be able to change the planet.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.429
To help you on your journey

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:17.440
today's message is "Don't
dwell on the past."

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.498
Over to you Joe Rogan.

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:20.948
(rooster crowing)

00:00:20.948 --> 00:00:23.160
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.429
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:29.819
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:29.819 --> 00:00:33.047
- Your life would feel better and richer

00:00:33.047 --> 00:00:35.402
if you had a goal, you chased that goal,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.491
you accomplished some things,

00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:38.361
and you would get this
boost of confidence.

00:00:38.361 --> 00:00:39.861
You'd get this boost of self esteem.

00:00:39.861 --> 00:00:41.711
Whatever it is that you're into doing.

00:00:41.711 --> 00:00:42.911
Maybe you're into drawing comic books.

00:00:42.911 --> 00:00:46.551
Maybe you're into making
pottery or sculpture.

00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:50.986
But find whatever the ff
that is, and pursue that

00:00:50.986 --> 00:00:52.001
instead of doing nothing.

00:00:52.001 --> 00:00:53.881
The people that are doing nothing,

00:00:53.881 --> 00:00:55.806
those are the real...

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:58.431
Look, doing something
might be as simple as like

00:00:58.431 --> 00:01:00.471
that Alex Honnold guy.

00:01:00.471 --> 00:01:01.621
He just climbs rocks,

00:01:01.621 --> 00:01:03.961
but he's world class climber
- [Man] It's somethin' though.

00:01:03.961 --> 00:01:04.794
- It's something.

00:01:04.794 --> 00:01:06.557
- One of the most common
questions that I get asked

00:01:06.557 --> 00:01:07.390
when I do interviews is

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.921
Evan, if you could go
back in a time machine

00:01:09.921 --> 00:01:12.081
and go talk to your 20 year old self,

00:01:12.081 --> 00:01:14.431
what message would you give yourself?

00:01:14.431 --> 00:01:17.611
And it's a question I always
have a hard time answering.

00:01:17.611 --> 00:01:19.841
I guess it's one of
those standard questions

00:01:19.841 --> 00:01:22.576
that people like to ask you
at the end of interviews.

00:01:22.576 --> 00:01:23.585
I have a hard time with it.

00:01:23.585 --> 00:01:26.201
One, because I'm so grateful
for where I am right now

00:01:26.201 --> 00:01:28.521
that I wouldn't really change anything.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.646
Everything that I went through

00:01:30.646 --> 00:01:32.931
has lead me to where I am right now,

00:01:32.931 --> 00:01:34.471
and I'm happy where I am right now,

00:01:34.471 --> 00:01:36.491
and so thank you for
all those experiences,

00:01:36.491 --> 00:01:39.041
even though some of them
may have been crappy.

00:01:39.041 --> 00:01:43.617
Two, I don't spend time
thinking about what didn't work,

00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:45.357
and spend time livin' in the past

00:01:45.357 --> 00:01:47.557
and I think to be an entrepreneur,

00:01:47.557 --> 00:01:50.427
to be enthusiastic, to be optimistic,

00:01:50.427 --> 00:01:52.737
to chase these dreams
that're goin' forward

00:01:52.737 --> 00:01:55.177
you can't do it when you're
just stuck in the past

00:01:55.177 --> 00:01:57.567
dwelling on all the mistakes
you made and how much you suck

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.837
and everything that
went wrong in your life.

00:01:59.837 --> 00:02:02.297
I've had a lot of negative
things that have happened to me

00:02:02.297 --> 00:02:04.277
but I don't remember them.

00:02:04.277 --> 00:02:05.417
I don't focus on them.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:07.997
One of the hardest exercises
I had when I first started

00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:10.202
workin' with a media coach was

00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:12.017
coming up with my foundation story

00:02:12.017 --> 00:02:13.587
and thinkin' about the hard times I had

00:02:13.587 --> 00:02:15.047
in my startup business

00:02:15.047 --> 00:02:16.887
when I was making the few
hundred dollars a month.

00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:18.357
I didn't even remember those stories.

00:02:18.357 --> 00:02:21.537
All the negative things that
happened to me just pfft.

00:02:21.537 --> 00:02:23.107
I don't think about them anymore.

00:02:23.107 --> 00:02:25.347
I think about what I'm focused on now,

00:02:25.347 --> 00:02:26.547
where I'm tryin' to go,

00:02:26.547 --> 00:02:28.507
and I get how those stories can help.

00:02:28.507 --> 00:02:29.957
They can help tell the journey.

00:02:29.957 --> 00:02:31.487
It can help with you
guys who are watching.

00:02:31.487 --> 00:02:33.587
Being able to access those things can help

00:02:33.587 --> 00:02:35.707
but I don't live there, anywhere close to

00:02:35.707 --> 00:02:38.837
on a weekly or monthly or
definitely not a daily basis.

00:02:38.837 --> 00:02:41.377
I just don't think about negative things

00:02:41.377 --> 00:02:42.317
that happened in the past.

00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:45.252
I think you'll see that
consistently with successful people.

00:02:45.252 --> 00:02:46.857
And then the third answer then becomes

00:02:46.857 --> 00:02:47.897
okay, I need to say something.

00:02:47.897 --> 00:02:50.707
I don't want to just tell
them that their question

00:02:50.707 --> 00:02:52.787
doesn't really touch me.

00:02:52.787 --> 00:02:54.237
The only think I come up with is

00:02:54.237 --> 00:02:57.357
I would just tell my younger
self to believe more.

00:02:57.357 --> 00:02:58.587
To believe in myself more.

00:02:58.587 --> 00:02:59.957
To believe in the mission more.

00:02:59.957 --> 00:03:02.007
To believe that I'm going
to do great things more.

00:03:02.007 --> 00:03:03.577
To believe that it's
going to work out more.

00:03:03.577 --> 00:03:07.432
But I wouldn't go and change
any of those specific things

00:03:07.432 --> 00:03:10.042
that a time machine might be able to fix.

00:03:10.042 --> 00:03:11.967
But the time machine doesn't exist

00:03:11.967 --> 00:03:14.467
so stop focusing on it, right?

00:03:15.337 --> 00:03:18.317
If the message is what would
I tell a young person today,

00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:19.487
I love that question.

00:03:19.487 --> 00:03:21.317
But what would I tell
myself from 20 years ago?

00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:22.525
I can't.

00:03:22.525 --> 00:03:24.046
I love possibilities.

00:03:24.046 --> 00:03:25.686
I love thinkin' about the future

00:03:25.686 --> 00:03:28.566
and things that are impossible
and how to fix that,

00:03:28.566 --> 00:03:31.776
but this is actually
impossible right now, right?

00:03:31.776 --> 00:03:34.456
There's no way to go back and
tell my younger self something

00:03:34.456 --> 00:03:35.786
so I don't focus on it.

00:03:35.786 --> 00:03:38.296
I don't care about it, I don't
want to go out and do it.

00:03:38.296 --> 00:03:41.206
If you gave me the option,
maybe that's a different choice

00:03:41.206 --> 00:03:43.891
but just livin' in the hypothetical

00:03:43.891 --> 00:03:47.202
and dwelling on the past
is not interesting to me.

00:03:47.202 --> 00:03:48.822
Again, if I look at this YouTube channel,

00:03:48.822 --> 00:03:50.432
we've had a lot of failed series.

00:03:50.432 --> 00:03:52.982
I've had a lot of videos
where I really sucked,

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:54.802
where my message was okay

00:03:54.802 --> 00:03:56.852
but my delivery was really terrible.

00:03:56.852 --> 00:03:59.262
I don't have a video
that I'm least proud of.

00:03:59.262 --> 00:04:00.552
I don't look at that video and say

00:04:00.552 --> 00:04:02.312
wow, that video's really terrible

00:04:02.312 --> 00:04:03.902
and it haunts me moving forward.

00:04:03.902 --> 00:04:05.812
I've had a lot series
that didn't work out.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:08.052
We recently canceled
the Believe Love series,

00:04:08.052 --> 00:04:10.292
which I loved and I found really useful

00:04:10.292 --> 00:04:11.582
but you guys didn't,

00:04:11.582 --> 00:04:14.182
so I might use that myself personally

00:04:14.182 --> 00:04:15.472
but not share it with you.

00:04:15.472 --> 00:04:17.252
There's been tons of other series though.

00:04:17.252 --> 00:04:20.992
We have a spot in our calendar
that is just for tests,

00:04:20.992 --> 00:04:23.537
where we're always testing new series,

00:04:23.537 --> 00:04:26.012
whether you guys agree to them or not.

00:04:26.012 --> 00:04:27.602
You guys liked them, you
want to share them or not.

00:04:27.602 --> 00:04:29.152
We had a series on morning routines.

00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:31.882
We had series on favorite
books from entrepreneurs.

00:04:31.882 --> 00:04:34.042
We had a series on, I
forget what we called it,

00:04:34.042 --> 00:04:37.152
where we compared two
contrasting points of view

00:04:37.152 --> 00:04:39.482
and said, hey find the line between them.

00:04:39.482 --> 00:04:41.382
And tons of other series
that I don't even remember.

00:04:41.382 --> 00:04:43.792
Even thinking about the
series that we canceled,

00:04:43.792 --> 00:04:45.219
I don't even care about it.

00:04:45.219 --> 00:04:47.679
I can't even access it
because I've just moved on.

00:04:47.679 --> 00:04:49.259
I encourage you to do the same.

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:51.149
So many people just live in their past.

00:04:51.149 --> 00:04:53.469
Because one thing didn't work out once,

00:04:53.469 --> 00:04:56.359
now nothin' is ever
going to work out again.

00:04:56.359 --> 00:04:58.939
You don't have to be the
accumulation of your history.

00:04:58.939 --> 00:05:01.564
You can set a new path for yourself.

00:05:01.564 --> 00:05:04.149
I would just try to spend
as much time as possible

00:05:04.149 --> 00:05:06.149
thinkin' about what you're doin' right now

00:05:06.149 --> 00:05:08.009
and thinkin' about where you want to go.

00:05:08.009 --> 00:05:10.049
Everything that happened, happened.

00:05:10.049 --> 00:05:11.409
Try to see the positive of it.

00:05:11.409 --> 00:05:13.089
It lead you to where you are right now.

00:05:13.089 --> 00:05:14.829
Be grateful for those experiences

00:05:14.829 --> 00:05:16.729
that guided you to be the
person you are right now

00:05:16.729 --> 00:05:18.289
and this vision that you
have to move foreword.

00:05:18.289 --> 00:05:20.349
That's it, move forward.

00:05:20.349 --> 00:05:22.779
Spend as much as your
mental energy as possible

00:05:22.779 --> 00:05:25.379
living in the present
and where you want to go

00:05:25.379 --> 00:05:27.739
and not dwell in the
things that happened to you

00:05:27.739 --> 00:05:28.969
'cause you can't change the past.

00:05:28.969 --> 00:05:30.789
The question today is, I'm curious.

00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:33.679
Is there something from your
past that is haunting you?

00:05:33.679 --> 00:05:36.579
An experience, a person,
a limiting belief?

00:05:36.579 --> 00:05:38.449
Something that is
haunting you and you feel

00:05:38.449 --> 00:05:41.119
is preventing you from moving
forward with your life,

00:05:41.119 --> 00:05:41.969
with your business?

00:05:41.969 --> 00:05:43.279
Leave it in the comments below.

00:05:43.279 --> 00:05:44.336
Release it.

00:05:44.336 --> 00:05:45.544
Let it free.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:48.619
Let it go, so that you can
focus on buildin' something

00:05:48.619 --> 00:05:49.549
way more positive.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.199
I want to see that in the comments.

00:05:51.199 --> 00:05:53.009
If you leave a comment
within the first couple hours

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:54.269
of this video goin' live,

00:05:54.269 --> 00:05:56.459
you might win one of our top
two prizes that come out daily.

00:05:56.459 --> 00:05:58.849
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Lazar Jovanovic.

00:05:58.849 --> 00:06:00.179
Thank you so much for picking up

00:06:00.179 --> 00:06:01.659
a copy of my book "Your One Word."

00:06:01.659 --> 00:06:03.339
It really, really means a lot to me

00:06:03.339 --> 00:06:05.074
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:06:05.074 --> 00:06:06.233
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:06.233 --> 00:06:07.303
I believe in you.

00:06:07.303 --> 00:06:09.223
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:09.223 --> 00:06:10.923
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:10.923 --> 00:06:13.553
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:13.553 --> 00:06:16.203
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:16.203 --> 00:06:18.293
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:06:18.293 --> 00:06:21.710
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:06:25.493 --> 00:06:29.763
- Well, the first time that I
really got involved in UFC was

00:06:29.763 --> 00:06:31.373
everybody had seen UFC 1.

00:06:31.373 --> 00:06:32.373
I saw UFC 1,

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.893
but when we got involved in those

00:06:35.893 --> 00:06:37.333
because we started taking jiu-jitsu.

00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:40.153
Through jiu-jitsu we fell
in love with the sport

00:06:40.153 --> 00:06:41.993
and we started to meet
some of the athletes.

00:06:41.993 --> 00:06:46.160
When I say "we," I mean me
and the Fertitta brothers.

00:06:47.186 --> 00:06:49.531
It was really learning about the sport

00:06:49.531 --> 00:06:50.611
and meeting the athletes

00:06:50.611 --> 00:06:55.326
that completely got us
literally addicted to the sport.

00:06:55.326 --> 00:06:58.061
When we went to our first ever UFC event,

00:06:58.061 --> 00:07:02.521
it was down in New Orleans
at the UNO Arena down there

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:05.191
and literally, me, Frank, and Lorenzo

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.311
were sitting in the
audience going, "Holy shh.

00:07:07.311 --> 00:07:10.011
"Imagine if they did this
and imagine if they did that?

00:07:10.011 --> 00:07:11.471
"This thing could be big."

00:07:11.471 --> 00:07:13.471
Then, once we bought it,

00:07:14.521 --> 00:07:17.188
our goal was and always has been

00:07:18.071 --> 00:07:20.321
to make this a global sport.

00:07:20.321 --> 00:07:22.048
- Go ahead, tell me what
your vision board looks like.

00:07:22.048 --> 00:07:24.648
Can you share some of the
things that're on there?

00:07:24.648 --> 00:07:26.208
- I used to have a
traditional vision board

00:07:26.208 --> 00:07:29.058
where you would take things that you want

00:07:29.058 --> 00:07:31.098
and put 'em up on poster
board, whatever, whatever.

00:07:31.098 --> 00:07:33.488
That's cool, I did that
when I did the seeker, but

00:07:33.488 --> 00:07:36.238
to me, the best vision
was the one you write down

00:07:36.238 --> 00:07:38.038
your long term or short term goals.

00:07:38.038 --> 00:07:39.678
Write down everything that
you want to accomplish

00:07:39.678 --> 00:07:41.738
and keep those things in your mind

00:07:41.738 --> 00:07:44.103
because your mind is what it makes

00:07:44.103 --> 00:07:45.573
it manifest in the reality.

00:07:45.573 --> 00:07:47.153
Your thoughts really do become things.

00:07:47.153 --> 00:07:50.253
I don't have a college
degree or anything like that.

00:07:50.253 --> 00:07:52.773
All I have is, back in 1998, I said

00:07:52.773 --> 00:07:54.533
I want to be a super jock.

00:07:54.533 --> 00:07:57.033
I said I want to be one of the
biggest radio personalities

00:07:57.033 --> 00:07:57.866
on the planet.

00:07:57.866 --> 00:08:02.033
I said I want to be in that
Wendy Williams, Tom Joyner,

00:08:02.993 --> 00:08:07.293
Doug Banks, Howard Stern,
you know, Bill O'Reilly,

00:08:07.293 --> 00:08:09.913
Rush Limbaugh, I want
to be in that number.

00:08:09.913 --> 00:08:11.150
When they think of Charlamagne,

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.440
I want them to think of me like that.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.880
I want to be my generation's that,

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.580
because all of those guys,

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.400
it's the natural cause that thing,

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.910
that power eventually fades or weakens.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.440
All of them, it's just like the NBA,

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.120
or music, it was the Magic
Johnson, Larry Bird era.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:25.310
There was Michael Jordan era.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.480
Now it's Lebron James era.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.220
That's just the way
things are in the game.

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:31.130
I knew that eventually it would be my time

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.670
if I wanted that, and so I claimed it.

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:36.650
My vision board is a
really just a notebook

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:39.660
with everything that I want in my life.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.080
- We always had this goal in sports.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.150
I give the credit to my coaches
for instilling that in me.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:47.940
It's like always creating this goal,

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.150
this part of time to achieve something.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.140
During that time nothing else mattered.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.130
It didn't matter what was
happening at school for me.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.120
It didn't happen what was
relationships didn't matter.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.190
It was just like achieving that goal.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.410
And maybe it comes back to
like childhood or something

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.380
where I just wanted to be a great athlete.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.900
When I get in that mind frame, I guess

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.360
I don't know, I just
want to achieve the goal

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.610
more than anything else.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.693
That's what I like to do.

